        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "c) Evaluative: Monitoring of this type is intended to be hardened in a professional and confidential manner and to document all aspects of the performance of the individual employee for evaluation purposes. Management personnel will conduct this type of monitoring. Evaluative call/interview monitoring will be from a sampling of call/interviews. Such calls/interviews will not be arbitrarily selected for evaluative purposes. The monitoring results should be reviewed with the employee within 10 business days after the monitoring has taken place. If the review is delayed for any reason, the employee may choose to have the monitoring tape discarded and receive an \"NA\" score for that tape, review the tape and results before deciding or have a new tape made.",
            "block_bbox": [
                47,
                74,
                629,
